---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import SakuraSpiral from '../components/SakuraSpiral.astro';
import SakuraFaller from '../components/SakuraFaller.astro';
import TerminalQuote from '../components/TerminalQuote.astro';

const nowText = 'Now: Using vibe coding to turn supply-chain ideas into working digital systems.';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me - Alex Huang"
	description="Alex Huang's vision for using vibe coding to accelerate practical supply-chain digitalization."
	pubDate={new Date('Jul 03 2026')}
	metaMode="page"
>
	<Fragment slot="background">
		<SakuraSpiral />
		<SakuraFaller density={1.8} heightVh={60} />
	</Fragment>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
		<p>
			I am Alex Huang. My vision is to use vibe coding&mdash;combining supply-chain knowledge,
			AI-assisted development, and rapid experimentation&mdash;to make supply-chain digitalization
			faster, more accessible, and grounded in real operational needs.
		</p>

		<h2>Vision</h2>
		<p>
			Supply chains still rely on fragmented data, repetitive coordination, and tools that are
			often too slow or expensive to adapt. I want to shorten the distance between an operational
			problem and a useful digital solution: describe the need, build a working prototype, learn
			from real users, and improve it continuously.
		</p>

		<h2>What I Am Building Toward</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Digital supplier-risk monitoring across delivery, price, quality, and external signals</li>
			<li>Smarter contract, forecasting, and decision-support workflows</li>
			<li>Small, composable tools that supply-chain teams can test and evolve quickly</li>
			<li>A practical vibe-coding workflow that connects domain experts directly with software creation</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Now</h2>
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-left">
			<TerminalQuote text={nowText} once={true} fixedHeight={false} />
		</div>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			The best way to reach me is via
			<a href="https://github.com/wublinux" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
